+// g-lab-bit fork (annot_ap_oc.patch)
+// Experimental API.
+// Put the appearance stream content of |annot| under optional content: every
+// object of the normal appearance gets nested marked content
+//   /OC /OCGn BDC ... EMC
+// one level per OCG in |ocg_indices| (indices into /OCProperties /OCGs;
+// ocg_indices[0] is the outermost, e.g. the top ancestor layer; duplicates
+// are ignored), and the appearance's /Resources get /Properties entries
+// referencing the groups. Viewers that ignore annotation /OC but honour marked
+// content (PDFium, PDFKit) then hide the markup when ANY of the groups is off,
+// through /OCProperties /D or FPDFDoc_SetOCGViewState(). Use together with
+// FPDFAnnot_SetOCMembership() for readers that use annotation /OC.
+//   appearance_mode - only FPDF_ANNOT_APPEARANCEMODE_NORMAL is supported.
+//   count           - 0 removes the /OC marks.
+// The appearance is regenerated from its page objects (as
+// FPDFAnnot_UpdateObject() does); existing /OC marks are replaced, other marks
+// are kept (the /OC levels are added inside them). Objects appended later
+// with FPDFAnnot_AppendObject() are not marked: call this again afterwards.
+// Supported for the subtypes FPDFAnnot_AppendObject() supports. Fails, without
+// changing anything, for an invalid index, a direct OCG, or an appearance
+// without its own /Resources.
+// FPDFDoc_DeleteOCG() does not remove these marks: re-mark the annotation
+// before deleting a group it uses.
+FPDF_EXPORT FPDF_BOOL FPDF_CALLCONV
+FPDFAnnot_SetAPOptionalContent(FPDF_DOCUMENT document,
+                               FPDF_ANNOTATION annot,
+                               FPDF_ANNOT_APPEARANCEMODE appearance_mode,
+                               const int* ocg_indices,
+                               int count);
+
 // Experimental API.
 // Get the total number of objects in |annot|, including path objects, text
 // objects, external objects, image objects, and shading objects.
